    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with a clear focal point in **Mickey Moniak**, who boasts our highest efficiency score at 75.75. **Mickey Moniak** benefits from a prime matchup against Michael King; the combination of a favorable park factor (+14%) and a strong platoon edge (+14%) makes him our must-start anchor. **Isaac Paredes** (69.54) serves as our second elite tier play, as he draws Seth Lugo in a matchup where the opposing xERA of 4.59 provides significant run-scoring potential. Both **Mickey Moniak** and **Isaac Paredes** are positioned to capitalize on their respective order slots, with **Isaac Paredes** receiving a notable boost from his #3 spot in the lineup.\n\nOur decision-making process for the utility spot was tight, with **Vinnie Pasquantino** (53.95) narrowly edging out marginal options despite facing a difficult arm in Ullola (2.71 xERA). While **Vinnie Pasquantino** carries a solid projection, he is battling a significant SP skill penalty (-19%), making him a lower-confidence play compared to the consistent production we expect from **Brice Turang** (54.17). **Brice Turang** earns his spot primarily through his #1 order assignment (+10%), which remains a key lever in our 5x5 format to maximize plate appearances for potential stolen base opportunities. **Moises Ballesteros** (54.94) and **Trevor Story** (48.15) round out the lineup, though both carry \"Lineup Pending\" tags, necessitating a final check before first pitch to ensure they remain in the spots we\u2019ve forecasted.\n\nWe are navigating a quiet day on the bench, as **Corbin Carroll**, **Josh Naylor**, and **James Wood** are all sidelined by team off-days, while **Tyler Soderstrom** remains on the IL. With the rest of our depth\u2014including **Jose Caballero**, **Austin Riley**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Seiya Suzuki**, **Gabriel Moreno**, **Max Muncy**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Cole Young**, **Griffin Conine**, **Edwin Arroyo**, and **Travis Bazzana**\u2014ei